<title>USA: Extended Stay to be listed on NYSE.</title>
<headline>Extended Stay to be listed on NYSE.</headline>
<dateline>FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Extended Stay America Inc said Friday its stock will begin trading Monday on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The company's shares will trade under the new symbol &quot;ESA&quot;. Extended Stay has been listed on Nasdaq since its initial public offering in December, 1995.</p>
<p>The company operates 108 extended stay lodging properties, including 39 Studio Plus Hotels, 68 Extended Stay America Efficiency Studios and one Crossland Economy Studios property, it said. It also has 103 facilities under construction and options to buy about 106 other sites for development.</p>
</text>
